:Namespace Chat
⍝ An APL client for the Exercise 4 chat, using WebSocketClient (supplied: you don't need to change this)
⍝ Usage:
⍝      2 ⎕FIX 'file://',#.WorkshopRoot,'/Exercises/Ex4-WebSockets/Chat.apln'
⍝      Chat.Join 'Ada'     ⍝ connect to ws://localhost:8084/chat and join as Ada
⍝      Chat.Say 'Hello'    ⍝ send a message; every message that arrives is printed in the session
⍝      Chat.Leave          ⍝ disconnect
⍝ 8094 Chat.Join 'Ada' connects to another port.

    (⎕IO ⎕ML)←1 1
    Client←⍬    ⍝ the WebSocketClient instance, once joined
    Messages←⍬  ⍝ every message received since joining, as namespaces, oldest first

    ∇ {ok}←{port}Join name;s;c;rc;msg;j
    ⍝ Connect to the chat server and join as name
    ⍝ ok - 1 if joined, 0 if there was a problem (the problem is printed)
      ok←0
      :If 0=⎕NC'port'
          port←8084
      :EndIf
      Leave ⍝ in case we're already connected
    ⍝ Create the client from a namespace of settings.
    ⍝ OnWSReceive names the function WebSocketClient calls for each message; it must be dyadic (see ShowMessage)
    ⍝ WaitTime (ms) is how long the listener waits at a time; Close waits for it, so a short WaitTime makes Leave quick
      s←⎕NS''
      s.(URL OnWSReceive WaitTime)←('ws://localhost:',(⍕port),'/chat')'#.Chat.ShowMessage' 1000
      c←#.WebSocketClient.New s
    ⍝ v20: c←#.WebSocketClient.New (URL: 'ws://localhost:',(⍕port),'/chat' ⋄ OnWSReceive: '#.Chat.ShowMessage' ⋄ WaitTime: 1000)
      :If 0≠c.rc ⍝ New reports problems (e.g. a misspelled setting gives rc ¯11) instead of signalling an error
          ⎕←'Problem: could not create the client: ',c.msg
          →0
      :EndIf
      (rc msg)←c.Connect
      :If rc≠0
          ⎕←'Problem: could not connect to ',c.URL,': ',msg
          ⎕←'Is the chat server running? Start it with: server←Run ',⍕port
          →0
      :EndIf
      Client←c
      Messages←⍬
      j←⎕NS''
      j.(type user)←'join'name
    ⍝ v20: j←(type: 'join' ⋄ user: name)
      ok←Send j
    ∇

    ∇ {ok}←Say text;j
    ⍝ Send a message to everyone in the chat
      j←⎕NS''
      j.(type text)←'msg'text
    ⍝ v20: j←(type: 'msg' ⋄ text: text)
      ok←Send j
    ∇

    ∇ Leave
    ⍝ Disconnect from the chat (the server tells everyone else you left)
      :If 9=⌊⎕NC'Client'
          {}Client.Close
          Client←⍬
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ ok←Send j;rc;msg
    ⍝ Send a namespace to the server as JSON
      ok←0
      :If 9≠⌊⎕NC'Client'
          ⎕←'Problem: not connected; use Chat.Join first'
          →0
      :EndIf
      (rc msg)←Client.Send 1 ⎕JSON j
      :If rc≠0
          ⎕←'Problem: could not send: ',msg
          →0
      :EndIf
      ok←1
    ∇

    ∇ client ShowMessage message;m
    ⍝ WebSocketClient calls this for each message received. It must be DYADIC:
    ⍝ client  - the WebSocketClient instance that received the message
    ⍝ message - namespace with buffer (the text received so far) and final (1 when the message is complete)
    ⍝ A monadic function here fails in WebSocketClient's listener thread, which silently closes the connection.
      :If message.final=1
          m←{0::⍬ ⋄ ⎕JSON ⍵}message.buffer
          :If 9=⌊⎕NC'm'
              Messages,←m
              ⎕←Format m
          :Else
              ⎕←'Received: ',message.buffer
          :EndIf
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ r←Format m;Get
    ⍝ One line of text for a message from the server, as the web page shows it
      Get←{6::'' ⋄ ⍵⍎⍺} ⍝ 'field' Get m, or '' if missing
      :Select 'type'Get m
      :Case 'msg' ⋄ r←('time'Get m),' ',('user'Get m),': ',('text'Get m)
      :Case 'join' ⋄ r←('time'Get m),' ',('user'Get m),' joined'
      :Case 'leave' ⋄ r←('time'Get m),' ',('user'Get m),' left'
      :Case 'error' ⋄ r←'Error: ',('text'Get m)
      :Else ⋄ r←1 ⎕JSON m
      :EndSelect
    ∇

:EndNamespace
